import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 442 | Dragon Ball · Zeno Setting Critique: The Arbitrariness of the Ultimate Being","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 442 | Dragon Ball · Zeno Setting Critique: The Arbitrariness of the Ultimate Being","no":442,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Zeno","Ultimate Being","Arbitrariness","Myriad-Ranks Republicanism","Law-First"],"related":["40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline","49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances","05-Myriad-Ranks Co-Progression Program"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0442_模块2-龙珠-全王设定批判-终极存在的随意性.md","filePath":"en/0442_模块2-龙珠-全王设定批判-终极存在的随意性.md"}'),a={name:"en/0442_模块2-龙珠-全王设定批判-终极存在的随意性.md"};function s(r,e,l,h,u,d){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-442-dragon-ball-·-zeno-setting-critique-the-arbitrariness-of-the-ultimate-being" tabindex="-1">Entry 442 | Dragon Ball · Zeno Setting Critique: The Arbitrariness of the Ultimate Being <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-442-dragon-ball-·-zeno-setting-critique-the-arbitrariness-of-the-ultimate-being" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 442 | Dragon Ball · Zeno Setting Critique: The Arbitrariness of the Ultimate Being&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 11) | Benchmark base: Documents 40, 49, 05</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-a-child-holds-an-eraser" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when a child holds an eraser <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-a-child-holds-an-eraser" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when a child holds an eraser&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Zeno is the apex of Dragon Ball worldview: one sentence and a universe vanishes; one wave and all villains are cleared away; he sits there like an innocent child, yet holds the power of life and death over twelve universes. This setting pushes &quot;the ultimate being&#39;s arbitrariness&quot; to the extreme — more terrifying than the God of Destruction&#39;s dictatorship is that above him there is a child who thinks &quot;playing games is enough.&quot; This entry takes the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> as core, dissecting the Zeno setting&#39;s institutional terror.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Zeno&#39;s energy is Dragon Ball worldview&#39;s absolute apex, but its direction is pure waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Game-style governance</strong>: Tournament of Power&#39;s essence is &quot;Zeno wants to watch fights&quot;; 8 universes eliminated just because &quot;Zeno feels there are too many&quot;</li><li><strong>Eraser-style clearing</strong>: Zamasu, Infinite Zamasu cleared by Zeno&#39;s single finger, not by trial, but because &quot;Zeno finds them annoying&quot;</li><li><strong>Childified ultimate power</strong>: Zeno looks like a child, acts like a child, decides like a child — but behind this childlike arbitrariness are Myriad Ranks&#39; billion-billion lives</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How Zeno&#39;s arbitrariness feeds historical regression:</p><ol><li><strong>No safety bottom line</strong>: any universe, any race does not know which day Zeno &quot;feels too many&quot; and wipes them out — civilization dares not do any long-term planning</li><li><strong>Law meaningless</strong>: Zeno&#39;s will above all law, all rules, all history — however perfect Myriad Ranks&#39; institutions, Zeno&#39;s one finger and they&#39;re gone</li><li><strong>Myriad Ranks completely powerless</strong>: facing Zeno, God of Destruction, Angels, Goku all can only &quot;smile along&quot;; Myriad Ranks do not even have a channel to express demands</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking in his relationship with Zeno:</p><ul><li><strong>Making friends with the ultimate dictator</strong>: Goku reaches out and says &quot;hello hello&quot; to Zeno; Zeno thus takes a liking to Goku — this &quot;friendship&quot; makes Zeno not lightly move Earth, but this protection is non-institutional, private affection</li><li><strong>Tournament of Power&#39;s wager</strong>: Goku proposes Tournament of Power, the wager is 8 universes&#39; survival — he treats Myriad Ranks&#39; fate as a chip for &quot;wanting to trade blows with the strong&quot;; Zeno is just playing along with him</li><li><strong>Accepting arbitrariness</strong>: Goku never questions &quot;by what right does Zeno decide universes&#39; survival,&quot; only thinks &quot;this kid is cute&quot; — this is the gifted&#39;s structural dependence on the ultimate dictator</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Zeno Arbitrariness</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Institutional Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Zeno&#39;s one finger clears universes</td><td>Symbiotic Constitution General Outline: universe survival goes legislative procedure; not tied to one person&#39;s one thought</td></tr><tr><td>Game-style governance</td><td>Anchor Council + Symbiotic Court; governance by law, not by game</td></tr><tr><td>No appeal, no accountability</td><td>Anchor Inspection Committee: supervise all cosmos-tier beings, including Zeno tier</td></tr><tr><td>Goku makes friends with Zeno</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republicanism: any individual, even Zeno tier, bound by law</td></tr><tr><td>Tournament of Power wager</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom: Myriad Ranks&#39; fate must not be gambled by any individual</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Zeno&#39;s power — 12 universes, Tournament of Power, Future Zamasu arc</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;if Zeno&#39;s power constrained by Anchor Council; universe survival by vote&quot; control</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count eliminated universes, Myriad-Ranks long-term construction rate, Myriad-Ranks trust in ultimate governance</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Zeno Arbitrariness Externality Report</em>, quantifying &quot;every time Zeno plays a game, how much life price Myriad Ranks pay&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: extremely low</strong>. Zeno &quot;supreme in all universes&quot; setting directly conflicts with early Supreme Kai &quot;creates universes&quot; setting — who creates universes? No one can say clearly</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: extremely high</strong>. Future Zeno, present Zeno, two Zenos, Zeno&#39;s attendants, number and relationships added with plot</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</strong>. Earth safety relies on Goku&#39;s private friendship with Zeno, not institutional guarantee</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: absolute apex energy used to play games; billion-billion lives treated as chips</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Zeno arbitrarily eliminates universes is predation of Myriad Ranks&#39; existence itself</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo however dictatorial only covers humans; Zeno&#39;s one finger wipes an entire universe</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad Ranks in front of Zeno do not even have qualification to &quot;be discussed&quot;</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Zeno treats &quot;multiverse&quot; as a chessboard to erase at will, not a Myriad-Ranks-co-built home</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Zeno setting is Dragon Ball worldview&#39;s most terrifying stroke — it tells readers the cosmos&#39;s apex is not justice, not law, not republic, but a child who thinks &quot;playing games is enough.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is simple: any individual, even strong enough to wipe a universe with one finger, must be bound by law; any governance, even by the ultimate being, must go through Myriad-Ranks parliament consent. Letting a child hold an eraser is not the cosmos&#39;s cuteness, it is the cosmos&#39;s tragedy.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · Zeno setting critique · the arbitrariness of the ultimate being described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./440_模块2-龙珠-破坏神设定批判-宇宙级存在的个人独裁.html">Entry 440 · God of Destruction</a> · <a href="./441_模块2-龙珠-天使设定批判-更高层级的恩赐制.html">Entry 441 · Angel Setting</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/40-共生宪法总纲.html">40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=i(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
